 * full checkout PAGE — inside a small `max-w-xl` modal. That UI mode is
 * designed to fill a whole page, not a compact dialog, and it is a
 * completely different, far-less-exercised code path than the Custom
 * Checkout (`ui_mode: "elements"`) build every other payment on this
 * platform (VPS/Hosting/Game/Email deploy wizards) already goes through —
 * hence the cramped, overlapping "Add $25.00 to your wallet" box the owner
 * screenshotted. Rather than patch that layout, this mounts the SAME
 * battle-tested Custom Checkout primitives PaymentStep.tsx uses
